Derived architecture
--------------------

The module decomposition (tag, length, object), the tag-class and universal-tag enums, and
several value-class ideas in this package were taken from the `ber` package of `snmpy`
(https://github.com/b1tninja/snmpy), Copyright (c) 2026 snmpy Contributors, distributed
under the MIT License. Four of its six test functions are re-expressed here as
`tests/test_snmpy_floor.py`, so behaviour its existing callers rely on cannot regress silently.
The two that are **not** ported are its `ObjectIdentifier` value-type tests, because this
package has no OID type yet (obligation `dk.oid`); claiming a complete floor would be worse
than admitting a short one.

**Only the architecture was carried over.** Every behaviour in this package is written
against VECTORS.md, because the code it descends from has eight measured defects, catalogued
in PLAN.md under "Defects that must be fixed, not moved". That distinction is not legal
pedantry: MIT's single condition is that the copyright notice and permission notice appear
in all copies or substantial portions of the software, so the text is reproduced below
rather than linked. The Apache-2.0 licence in LICENSE governs this package as a whole; where
the two interact, nothing here grants a recipient fewer rights than MIT grants for the
derived portions.

